# MSYS/Cygwin bash writes a crash dump into whatever directory it died in. One of
# these was committed and then deployed to $HOME on every machine, so keep them
# out of the repo. .chezmoiignore covers the other half: not deploying one that
# happens to be sitting in the source tree.
*.stackdump

# herdr-lazy rewrites this on every sync. The plugin *list* is the single
# authority for what should be installed; the resolved commits are local tool
# state, not intent, and pinning them would make `sync` revert plugins to old
# commits instead of taking what is current.
herdr/plugins.lock
